        "content": "<p>rvolosatovs opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14626\">PR #14626</a> from <code>rvolosatovs:fix/err-ctx-align</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><code>error-context.debug-message</code> bounds-checked the guest-provided destination pointer for the string's <code>(ptr, len)</code> pair, but not its alignment, and then wrote the pair via<br>\n<code>&lt;str as Lower&gt;::linear_lower_to_memory</code>, which <code>debug_assert!</code>s that the offset is 4-byte aligned. A guest passing an in-bounds but misaligned pointer could therefore panic the host in debug builds, while release builds performed the unaligned write.</p>\n<p>Check the pointer's alignment before lowering and trap with \"invalid debug message pointer: not aligned\", the same way the stream/future read and write paths in this file report misaligned pointers.</p>\n</blockquote>",
